---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
const updated = new Date(SITE.policyUpdated + 'T12:00').toLocaleDateString('en-US', { dateStyle: 'long' });
const host = new URL(SITE.url).host;
---

<TextPage
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`How ${SITE.name} (operated by ${SITE.operator}) handles information: calculators run in your browser, plus cookies, analytics, advertising and your rights.`}
  h1="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p><strong>Last updated: {updated}</strong></p>

  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    Welcome to {SITE.name} (<a href={SITE.url}>{host}</a>), a website operated by {SITE.operator} (“we”, “us”, “our”). We respect your privacy and are committed
    to protecting the personal information of visitors who use our website and online calculators.
  </p>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains what information may be collected when you visit our website, how it may be used, how it is protected, and what choices
    you have. By accessing or using our website, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <h3>2.1 Personal information</h3>
  <p>We may collect personal information when you voluntarily:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Contact us by email.</li>
    <li>Submit feedback or suggestions.</li>
    <li>Report errors or technical problems.</li>
    <li>Request help with our services.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This information may include your name, email address and the contents of your message.</p>

  <h3>2.2 Non-personal information</h3>
  <p>When you visit our website, certain technical information may be collected automatically by our hosting provider or, where enabled, analytics tools, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Internet Protocol (IP) address.</li>
    <li>Browser type and version.</li>
    <li>Device and operating system information.</li>
    <li>Pages visited and the date and time of visits.</li>
    <li>Referring website addresses.</li>
    <li>General website usage statistics.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This information helps us understand website performance and improve the user experience.</p>

  <h2>3. Calculator Information and Your Inputs</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} provides free online calculators. <strong>All calculations run directly in your web browser.</strong> The numbers and values you type into
    our calculators are not sent to or stored on our servers.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Share links:</strong> if you use the “Share link” button, your inputs are added to the page address (URL) so the link can recreate your
      result. Anyone you send that link to can see those inputs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Calculator history:</strong> the scientific calculator on our home page saves your recent calculations and your degree/radian setting in your
      browser’s local storage, on your own device, so they are still there next time. You can delete individual items with the × button, remove all of them
      with “Clear all”, or clear this website’s data in your browser settings. This data is never sent to us.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Even so, we recommend that you avoid entering sensitive personal, financial, medical or confidential information into any online tool unless it is
    necessary.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
  <p>Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to improve functionality and understand how visitors use our services. Cookies may be used for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Essential website functionality.</li>
    <li>Remembering your preferences.</li>
    <li>Website analytics and performance monitoring.</li>
    <li>Advertising and measurement.</li>
    <li>Improving website usability.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can manage or disable cookies in your browser settings. Disabling some cookies may affect certain features. Where the law requires it, we will ask
    for your consent before using non-essential cookies or similar technologies.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Third-Party Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>Our website may display advertisements from third-party advertising networks, including Google AdSense. These providers may use cookies, web beacons or similar technologies to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Display advertisements.</li>
    <li>Measure advertising performance.</li>
    <li>Limit how often you see the same advertisement.</li>
    <li>Provide personalised or non-personalised advertising, depending on your settings and applicable consent requirements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites. Google’s use of advertising
    cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to our site and/or other sites on the Internet.
  </p>
  <p>
    Learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services at
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">policies.google.com/technologies/ads</a>. You can opt out of
    personalised advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">adssettings.google.com</a>, or opt out of some
    third-party vendors’ use of cookies at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info/choices</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Analytics and Website Performance</h2>
  <p>We may use third-party analytics services, such as Google Analytics, to understand website traffic. These services may collect information such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Number of visitors.</li>
    <li>Pages viewed and time spent on pages.</li>
    <li>Traffic sources.</li>
    <li>Device and browser information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use these insights to improve our calculators, website performance and user experience.</p>

  <h2>7. Third-Party Services and External Links</h2>
  <p>
    Our pages link to external websites, such as the government agencies and research we cite as sources. We may also use third-party services for hosting,
    analytics, advertising, security and website functionality. These third parties process information under their own privacy policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    {SITE.operator} does not control the privacy practices or content of external websites. We encourage you to review the privacy policy of any website you
    visit.
  </p>

  <h2>8. How We Use Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide and maintain our online calculators.</li>
    <li>To respond to questions and support requests.</li>
    <li>To improve website functionality and performance.</li>
    <li>To understand visitor preferences and website usage.</li>
    <li>To detect and prevent spam, fraud and security threats.</li>
    <li>To comply with applicable legal obligations.</li>
    <li>To manage advertising and measure website performance.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use personal information only for legitimate purposes and in accordance with applicable privacy laws.</p>

  <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information against unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure or destruction. Our
    website is served over an encrypted HTTPS connection. However, no method of transmitting or storing data over the Internet is completely secure, so we
    cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes in this policy, subject to legal requirements. If you have sent us
    personal information and want it deleted, contact us using the details below. We will review and process eligible requests in accordance with applicable
    laws and verification requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children’s Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is intended for a general audience and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children without
    any consent required by law. If you believe a child has provided personal information to us inappropriately, please contact us so we can investigate and
    take appropriate action.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live and the laws that apply, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Request access to your personal information.</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate information.</li>
    <li>Request deletion of eligible personal information.</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
    <li>Object to or restrict certain processing.</li>
    <li>Lodge a complaint with the appropriate data-protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise these rights, contact us using the details below.</p>

  <h2>13. International Visitors</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} can be accessed from many countries. Depending on your location, your information may be processed in countries other than your own. We take
    reasonable steps to handle personal information in line with applicable data-protection requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be published on this page with a new “Last updated” date. Please review it periodically.</p>

  <h2>15. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>If you have questions, concerns or requests about this Privacy Policy, contact us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Website operator:</strong> {SITE.operator}</li>
    <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href={SITE.url}>{host}</a></li>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>We appreciate your feedback and will make reasonable efforts to respond to privacy-related enquiries.</p>
</TextPage>
